  "headline": "Indonesia Reports State Budget Deficit Of Rp379 Trillion By October",
  "seoTitle": "Indonesia State Budget Deficit Rp379 Trillion",
  "metaDescription": "The Indonesian government reported a budget deficit of Rp379.3 trillion as of October 2026, amid ongoing fiscal management and economic strategy discussions.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Indonesia's state budget deficit reached Rp379.3 trillion by October 2026, equivalent to 1.47 percent of the national GDP.",
    "Finance officials maintain that a budget deficit does not equate to a financial loss, emphasizing the role of the APBN in national development.",
    "The government is currently integrating the state budget with the Danantara Investment Management Agency to bolster national economic growth."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian Ministry of Finance has reported a state budget (APBN) deficit of Rp379.3 trillion as of October 2026, representing 1.47 percent of the national gross domestic product. Government officials, including Finance Minister Suahasil Nazara, have clarified that this deficit is a planned instrument for economic support rather than a financial loss. As the Prabowo Subianto administration enters its second year, fiscal policy remains focused on balancing the 2027 state budget to promote public welfare and economic stability. Recent efforts have centered on budget efficiency and strategic coordination between the APBN and the newly established Danantara Investment Management Agency. Concurrently, the government continues to monitor various economic sectors, noting performance indicators in customs and excise revenue, which reached Rp267.2 trillion by October, alongside developments in the mining, oil and gas, and public infrastructure transportation sectors.",
